EXAMPLE MODULE (SAMPLE)
----------------------
Module: Introduction to JavaScript
Duration: 2 hours

Learning Objectives:
□ Understand basic JavaScript syntax
□ Learn about variables and data types
□ Write simple JavaScript programs

Lessons:
1. JavaScript Basics
   Type: Video + Text
   Duration: 30 minutes
   Content:
   "What is JavaScript?
   JavaScript is a programming language that powers the web..."
   
   Video URL: [Your video URL]
   
   Quiz:
   Question: "Which keyword is used to declare a variable in modern JavaScript?"
   A) var
   B) let
   C) const
   D) All of the above
   Correct Answer: D
   Explanation: "Modern JavaScript provides three ways to declare variables..."

2. Variables and Data Types
   Type: Code
   Duration: 45 minutes
   Code Exercise:
   // Initial Code
   let name = "";
   let age = 0;
   
   // Write code to print "My name is [name] and I am [age] years old"
   
   // Expected Output:
   // "My name is John and I am 25 years old"

Module Assignment:
Title: "Create a Simple Calculator"
Description: "Build a calculator that can perform basic arithmetic operations"
Instructions: "Create functions for addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division..."
Submission Type: Code
Total Points: 100

Note: This template is a guide. Adjust sections based on your course needs. 